y, pan-fried fish with quick vegetables, an omelette, or pasta with a sauce made while the water boils."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I keep food warm without drying it out?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Hold cooked dishes in an oven at about 70&deg;C, covered with foil or a lid, for up to thirty minutes. Warm the plates in the same oven; a hot plate keeps food warm at the table for much longer."}}]}]}</script>
